---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Koate Kpai and this multi-cloud engineering blog.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I'm Koate Kpai, a multi-cloud platform and AI implementation engineer. This
      site documents production-grade architecture across <strong>AWS, GCP, and
      Azure</strong> — Terraform and Bicep, Cloud Run, GKE, EKS, Fargate, SRE,
      security and IAM, data/MLOps, and FinOps — with an active focus on AI on
      Microsoft Foundry (RAG pipelines, agents, retrieval, and evaluation).
    </p>
    <p>
      Every post is code-first and backed by evidence: working Terraform,
      Bicep, GitHub Actions, and Python, real command output, metrics, and cost.
      The goal is simple: patterns you can actually run, not slideware.
    </p>
    <h2>How posts are organised</h2>
    <p>
      Posts live under seven pillars (A–G) and are tagged with a cloud track —
      <strong>AWS, GCP, Azure, or Multi</strong> (the cross-cloud bridge series
      maps one technique across clouds). Each post carries a proof tier: Tier 1
      runs live infrastructure, Tier 2 proves with code and commands, and Tier 3
      is a reference architecture. Org-dependent topics are flagged and
      scheduled last.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browse by pillar, by cloud, or by tag. Subscribe via
      <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
